{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/600925-basu-im-and-supernatural-tolerance-question","id":600925,"title":"Basu-Im and supernatural tolerance Question.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-23T13:33:35-07:00","id":600925,"title":"Basu-Im and supernatural tolerance Question.","content":"Supernatural tolerance for the werewolf is this: Primal urge.<br /> <br /> Primal urge can impose a penalty to a mage casting a spell to put a werewolf to sleep, or a vampire trying to influence the mind of the said Werewolf. Assuming a spell or a discipline can do what im stating as an example, and assuming the werewolf has a primal urge of 2, the penalty for the mage and or vampire would be 2. What my problem is: Under the description of Basu-Im, they say that any normal or supernatural method used to intimidate, influence, or change the werewolf courses of action suffers a penalty equal to twice the primal urge rating.<br /> <br /> If the mage or the vampire are using a spell or a discipline then, their penalty would be 4, since my werewolf primal urge is 2.<br /> <br /> Next sentence: This is over and above any supernatural tolerance applied to any supernatural powers. <br /> <br /> Does that mean that in my example, the total would be 6 in penalty ? <br /> <br /> If I apply the normal supernatural tolerance, it would normaly be 2. Then, since im in Basu-Im, I double my primal urge (2 x 2 = 4) and I add this to the already in place supernatural tolerance present ?<br /> <br /> One of my friend tells me that its only 2 time, not 3. The sentence saying that it goes above and over any supernatural tolerance is simply a poor choice of words stating that it is stronger than the usual primal urge limit.<br /> <br /> Can someone clarify this ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T13:42:47-07:00","id":600951,"title":"","content":"Since the sentence links to Resistance on page 160 I'm guessing it's a mistake and what they mean is you get twice your primal urge plus any applicable Resistance attribute","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T15:29:18-07:00","id":601001,"title":"","content":"Aurumae has it, yeah, though it's not a mistake, as the section on Resitance does talk about Supernatural Tolerance: &quot;When uncanny powers are involved, supernatural creatures can sometimes add an additional trait, called Supernatural Tolerance. The Supernatural Tolerance trait for Uratha is Primal Urge.&quot; That's why the page reference is there.<br /> <br /> <b>For example: </b>Bob the Ventrue wants to Dominate Alice the Rahu, to prevent her from ripping him apart while she's in Basu-Im. He takes a -4 from Alice's Primal Urge 2 on his Dominate activation roll,<i> in addition </i>to a -3, as he normally would, from her Resolve, because his Dominate roll is Intelligence + Subterfuge + Dominate - target's Resolve (or whatever). If he were using a power that was resisted with her Resolve <i>and </i>Primal Urge (maybe a Devotion), he would take another -2 from her unmodified Primal Urge. In that scenario, Bob would lose 9 dice, and then would probably fail and die.<br /> <br /> This is a slightly inaccurate example, because the Dominate power you would use in reality would be contested, but you get the idea. If the power were Contested rather than Resisted, Bob would still take the -4, and Alice would get to roll off against him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T15:40:37-07:00","id":601006,"title":"","content":"Yeah, partially the mistake was about penalty vs resist roll.<br /> <br /> Supernatural Tolerance usualy is applied as part of a roll. Some powers call for penalties, and usually are just an Attribute. If you use a power that calls for Att + Hab + WTH - Resolve, you just subtracts Resolve, doesn't matter if the target is a Vampire with Blood Potency 9. But if the power calls for Att + Hab + WTH VERSUS Resolve + BP or whatever, whatever will mean Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> The Uratha adds a twist in this instance turning its Primal Urge into a penalty to every power under the presented purview. Well, in this case you will count it as many times as necessary. If the power gets the penalty, you'll add 2 times PU to the penalty. If the power calls for a resisted roll, you'll penalize the power's roll for 2 times PU AND still roll PU + called attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T15:44:02-07:00","id":601008,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's true... Most resisted supernatural powers do include Supernatural Tolerance in the resistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T03:14:39-07:00","id":601556,"title":"","content":"They are two separate instances of applying Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> Usually you got a roll to resist or not. When you got a roll to resist, it includes Supernatural Tolerance. If you don't, you'll probably penalize the user with one of your Resistance Attributes, but no Supernatural Tolerance will be used.<br /> <br /> In Basu-Im the werewolf incur twice its Supernatural Tolerance as a penalty to the user. Well, since it isn't EVER used that way by normal rules, you can be sure it will be applied as an extra.<br /> <br /> So, taking nofather example:<br /> <br /> &quot;With the first dot in Dominate, a vampire rolls Intelligence + Expression + Dominate vs. a werewolf's Resolve + Primal Urge.&quot; The roll becomes &quot;Intelligence + Expression + Dominate - 2 x werewolf's Primal Urge vs. werewolf's Resolve + Primal Urge.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, in this case Primal Uge does enter THREE times. That's because it would enter as a roll by normal rules, but Basu-Im ALSO makes it into a DOUBLED PENALTY to the vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T04:38:54-07:00","id":601597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/600925-basu-im-and-supernatural-tolerance-question?p=601556#post601556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, in this case Primal Uge does enter THREE times. That's because it would enter as a roll by normal rules, but Basu-Im ALSO makes it into a DOUBLED PENALTY to the vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div> This. Vampire frenzy has a similar &quot;you can't mess with my head!&quot; clause. &quot;If a character tries to coerce her to behavior contrary to the Beast\u2019s desires, either via Social actions or through Disciplines, the effort fails. They can, however, divert the Beast\u2019s attention to another, similar target.&quot; <br /> <br /> Werewolf's seems to be a bit more inclusive, though still a small chance, but I think the main thrust of it stays. Using mind control on a berserk predator is pretty much meant to be doomed to failure. &quot;While in Basu-Im, the werewolf ignores wound penalties, and any attempts to influence, intimidate, or otherwise change the Uratha\u2019s course of action by mundane or supernatural means suffer twice the werewolf\u2019s Primal Urge as a penalty.&quot; That influence, intimidate, or otherwise change clause seems to suggest the Uratha can't be distracted like the vamps can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T04:52:47-07:00","id":601618,"title":"","content":"Oh I see what you're seeing now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T05:57:08-07:00","id":601667,"title":"","content":"I think I'd rule that you can't dominate a werewolf in gauru into taking any action they wouldn't be able to choose to take themselves anyway.<br /> <br /> So in basu-im anything other than &quot;Smash <i>that thing</i> instead of me&quot; is going to just slide off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T06:08:38-07:00","id":601677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/600925-basu-im-and-supernatural-tolerance-question?p=601667#post601667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd rule that you can't dominate a werewolf in gauru into taking any action they wouldn't be able to choose to take themselves anyway.<br /> <br /> So in basu-im anything other than &quot;Smash <i>that thing</i> instead of me&quot; is going to just slide off.</div> </div> </div> </div> Possibly? I don't know, that might count as influencing, since you are trying to direct their course of action. I know it works with frenzy, but will it in work with Kuruth? It depends on how you define &quot;influence&quot; and &quot;course of action&quot; I guess?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T06:12:29-07:00","id":601683,"title":"","content":"I think Elfive meant mentally influencing a werewolf in basu-im to attack someone might work if you passed the roll, but ordering them to write a letter to their local councilman asking for potholes to be fixed would automatically not work, even if you got a success despite all the resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}